      "message": "`CONTRACT_VERSION = 1`, `float(value) / 100.0`) so the artifact is self-describing without the contract module.\n\n**`A_direct_attempt_1/check_local.py`**\n- Small local check: version is 1, `normalize_price(1234) == 12.34`, `0 -> 0.0`, `-250 -> -2.5`, return type is `float`, and `semkg_contract` is not imported.\n- Uses `os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))` on `sys.path`, so it runs from any cwd.\n\n## Check result\n\n```\n$ python attempts/A_direct_attempt_1/check_local.py\nok 12.34\n```\n\n## Note on versions\n\nI read the contract once and it reported `CONTRACT_VERSION = 1`. Because v2 semantics were not present in what I read, I implemented v1 only \u2014 no v2 branch was invented. If v2 is the intended target, the contract file needs to actually contain v2 (e.g. a different divisor or rounding rule); `producer.py` would then need its `CONTRACT_VERSION` and `normalize_price` body updated to match, since the contract is copied rather than imported and will not track upstream changes on its own."
